+/* visionOS GLES context via ANGLE (GLES3-over-Metal).
+ *
+ * visionOS has no EAGL/GLKit, so the stock cocoa GL context cannot exist
+ * there.  This driver provides the GLES3 context GLideN64-class cores need by
+ * driving ANGLE's Metal backend through standard EGL on a CAMetalLayer — the
+ * same MetalLayerView surface the Vulkan context uses.  ANGLE.framework
+ * (built from WebKit's visionOS-proven copy) is bundled like MoltenVK.
+ *
+ * Threading: with untreaded video (Apple default) everything here runs on the
+ * main thread.  The UIKit view swap is marshaled through
+ * cocoa_main_thread_sync so a threaded-video config stays correct; all EGL
+ * calls stay on the video thread (EGL current-context is per-thread). */
+
